  <prompt>Owner UAT round 10 (2026-10-07), items 1-3. Record: `notes/042-uat-round10-2026-10-07.md`.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE frontend developer on the Office add-in (React 19, Fluent UI v9).</role>

  <goal>Expand/Collapse is always visible at the toolbar's right end; both hosts show icon-only tabs at a normal width and labels when wide; Word's expand keeps the document in view.</goal>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner item 1">Closest feasible to "next to the ✕": the host title row cannot hold an add-in button; Expand right-most in the toolbar, never hidden in "⋮".</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner item 2">Same label rule in Word and Outlook; icon-only items keep names (NFR-11).</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner item 3">Expanded pane well short of the whole window on desktop.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Tests for the label rule, positions and the new expand candidates.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Word and Outlook at ~395 px: icon-only tabs with names; at 640: labels.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Expand/Collapse is the right-most toolbar button at every width.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Desktop expand requests 2x default capped at 35% of the screen; web caps at half the window and 500.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Gates: full jest green; lint 0; typecheck 0 production; test-file debt not above the pin.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step>Rewrite useToolbarFit as a width-based label rule with the overflow guard.</step>
    <step>Toolbar: Expand right-most, no menu item.</step>
    <step>Expand candidates 2x / 35% screen / 85% step.</step>
    <step>Tests; gates; notes; status.</step>
  </steps>

  <justification>
    <existing>Toolbar, useToolbarFit (107), taskPaneWidthService (103/104).</existing>
    <extension>Yes — all three are modified; nothing new.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Owner UAT round 10: Expand hidden in a menu, hosts look different, and the expanded pane covers the document.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

